      "writtenOn": "2026-01-14T18:35:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this should now be resolved, thanks for the suggestion, code is much much cleaner.",
      "parentUuid": "67974492_18675703",
      "revId": "c9e72f2fccb2228dee077361daa5f15bca463a21",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "33cb6add_43509a8f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-14T19:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We could do that without this class at all, simply using Class.forName() would suffice.\n\nThat\u0027s not true. Serialization is a whole separate thing and that is what\u0027s ultimately needed for multi-site, as noted in [Luca\u0027s comment](https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/gerrit/+/540181/comment/f7d90a88_cb217d35/). There\u0027s a whole set of classes for cache serialization in `java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/serialize/` and they only work for persisted caches because those have [builder methods](https://gerrit.googlesource.com/gerrit/+/refs/changes/81/540181/15/java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/PersistentCacheProvider.java#84) to set the key \u0026 value serializers.\n\n\u003e but just to ensure that we expect to be loading specific classes...\n\nYou\u0027re still trusting that any class registered as a key in a cache is \"safe\". How is that improving anything?",
      "parentUuid": "741fe0d1_b5442d61",
      "revId": "c9e72f2fccb2228dee077361daa5f15bca463a21",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17cdb25c_8b2d7fef",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-14T21:53:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e You\u0027re still trusting that any class registered as a key in a cache is \"safe\". How is that improving anything?\n\nAny class name retrived from a network payload isn\u0027t safe by definition. Any class installed on the Gerrit server in the `/plugins` or `/lib` directory has to be considered as safe, as it is already in the Gerrit JVM :-)",
      "parentUuid": "33cb6add_43509a8f",
      "revId": "c9e72f2fccb2228dee077361daa5f15bca463a21",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb1c8d4a_01c0191e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-14T22:04:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e You\u0027re still trusting that any class registered as a key in a cache is \"safe\". How is that improving anything?\n\u003e \n\u003e Any class name retrived from a network payload isn\u0027t safe by definition. Any class installed on the Gerrit server in the `/plugins` or `/lib` directory has to be considered as safe, as it is already in the Gerrit JVM :-)\n\nWhere are you worried about loading classes from?\n\nI\u0027m not trying to be rude or difficult. I don\u0027t think you\u0027re forming a logical argument here. It\u0027s not like a class name is enough to load some random JAR with that class from the internet. If that class isn\u0027t already in your JVM ClassLoader, it fails to instantiate. I don\u0027t see any change in security posture as a result of what this change proposes.",
      "parentUuid": "17cdb25c_8b2d7fef",
      "revId": "c9e72f2fccb2228dee077361daa5f15bca463a21",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
